<title>JAPAN: Kansai Electric says nuclear plant checks on track.</title>
<headline>Kansai Electric says nuclear plant checks on track.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kansai Electric Power Co Inc said on Thursday that its 826,000-kilowatt (kw) nuclear power plant in Mihama, on the Sea of Japan coast, will complete scheduled maintenance around the end of February.</p>
<p>The No 3 power plant has been shut down since August 27 for regular maintenance checks, the company said in a news release. It said that the power plant was due to resume operations around the end of February, in line with the initial schedule.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-5473-3706</p>
